course: dictionary
lesson: 8486
title: One word, three meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A word can have more than one meaning. «Sandbox» is one word with three different meanings. Read the words around it to find out which meaning the writer wants.
explain: In a park, a sandbox is a box or pit filled with sand where small children play. In computing, a sandbox is a safe, closed space where a program can run without harming the rest of the computer. In gaming, sandbox mode means free play without strict goals.
explain: «Gorse, broom and Himalayan balsam have pods that dry and twist on hot dry days until they burst and fling the seeds out, and the sandbox tree flings its seeds at around 250 km per hour.» The clues are pods, bursting and flinging seeds. These clues show that the sandbox here is a tree, not a box of sand or a computer space.
fact: Context means the words and sentences around a word.
fact: «Sandbox» can mean a play pit, a safe space in computing, or free-play mode in a game.
fact: In the UK and Australia, a play sandbox is called a sandpit.
fact: «Sandbox mode» means free play without strict goals.
fact: In «the sandbox tree flings its seeds», the clues show that sandbox is the name of a tree.
exercise: «Little children were digging and building in the sandbox at the park.» What is a sandbox in this sentence? | *A box or pit filled with sand for children to play in | A game where players build freely | A safe space where a program can run | A tree that flings its seeds
exercise: The new app was tested in a sandbox, so it could not harm the computer's files. What does sandbox mean here? | A pit filled with sand | *A safe, closed space where a program can run | A playground slide | A type of wooden box for toys
exercise: Ben chose sandbox mode and built whatever he liked, with no rules or goals. What does sandbox mode suggest? | *Free play without strict goals | A race to the finish line | Sleeping in a box of sand | A strict test with a timer
test: «The sandbox tree flings its seeds at around 250 km per hour.» What do the words around sandbox tell you? | The sandbox is a box filled with sand | The sandbox is a kind of car | The sandbox is a computer space | *The sandbox is a tree that flings seeds
test: Mia says, «My sandbox is at the playground.» In the UK or Australia, what might she call it? | A sandbox game | A sandbox mode | A sandbag | *A sandpit
exam: Ella reads, «Keep the unknown file in the sandbox so it cannot damage your computer.» What does sandbox mean, and which clues helped you decide? | *A safe, closed space for a program, because cannot damage your computer shows it is about computing | A tree, because seeds are mentioned | A game with free play, because it is fun | A box of sand, because children play in it
